  "slug": "quantum-adapted-fddb",
  "summary": "Spin-adapted sampling and MPS loading yield exact symmetry sectors while sparse and first-quantised methods cut sample and Toffoli costs.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is encoding physical structure to reduce quantum simulation cost, with symmetry as the clearest case. Spin-adapted SqDRIFT completes sampled configurations to enforce S^2 and return exact spin eigenstates. A circuit loads U(1)×SU(2)-symmetric matrix product states from spin-adapted reduced tensors, cutting Toffoli counts for fault-tolerant algorithms. Other items exploit structure differently: sparse quantum prolate diagonalization uses compressed sensing to reduce sample complexity from O(N_s) to O(log N_s) with a trapped-ion demonstration, a sum-of-squares representation lowers first-quantised phase estimation Toffoli cost by up to 16x, and a canonical polyadic decomposition of Coulomb-like potentials reduces T-gate scaling. On the classical side, F2-linear partitioning enables Pauli propagation beyond 10^11 strings. Quantum-walk search on complete bipartite graphs is also realized on hardware.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-23"
}
